    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Every subatomic particle has an electrical charge relative to the proton's charge, which is assigned the value <strong>+1</strong>. Protons carry a <strong>positive charge (+1)</strong>, electrons carry a <strong>negative charge (-1)</strong>, and neutrons carry <strong>no charge (0)</strong>. This relative charge scale helps us understand electrical neutrality and ion formation.</p>",
